## §4 — AgentEvent (High-Level Event Stream)

```go
package core

type AgentEvent interface {
    eventMarker()  // sealed — product layer type-switches
    Timestamp() time.Time
}

type (
    MessageStart   struct{ MessageID string; Role Role }
    MessageDelta   struct{ MessageID string; ContentDelta string }
    MessageEnd     struct{ MessageID string }
    ToolCallStart  struct{ CallID, ToolName string; Args json.RawMessage }
    ToolCallUpdate struct{ CallID string; Partial PartialResult }
    ToolCallEnd    struct{ CallID string; Result ToolResult }
    TurnStart      struct{ TurnID string }
    TurnEnd        struct{ TurnID string; Reason TurnEndReason }
    ErrorEvent     struct{ Err error; Code ErrorCode }
)
```

**Design rationale**:
- **Sealed interface** (`eventMarker()` private method). Product layer type-switches are compiler-guaranteed exhaustive. Adding a new event type requires changing the core package — enforced design review (C2/R6).
- **Not raw `ProviderEvent`** (A2 #3: shrink boundary). Token deltas are consumed inside Loop; product layer only sees merged `MessageDelta`.
- **`ToolCallUpdate` ordering caveat**: In parallel tool batches, partial and final events may arrive out of order. Product layers needing strict ordering should self-sort by `CallID + seq`.

**Divergence from pi**: Pi's `AssistantMessageEvent` served both raw-provider and product-layer subscribers. Tau enforces double-layer separation.

